<Item XName="Note1" UserName="Note1" Type="Notes">
<Description>Radar System Simulation</Description>
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in&quot; class=MsoTitle align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;RADAR System Simulation&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;This&amp;nbsp;workspace provides several simple examples for&amp;nbsp;basic&amp;nbsp;Radar system simulation.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Example1 - PulseRadar&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;Basic models generate a pulse signal, upconvert it, and downconvert it again. This simple block diagram is useful as a template.&amp;nbsp; &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Example2 - ChirpRadar &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;Chirp signal is&amp;nbsp;formed by using basic subnetwork model.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Users can open the Chirp signal model and modify it as needed to create custom model for&amp;nbsp;their own&amp;nbsp;system.&amp;nbsp; In this design, a radar channel model is included&amp;nbsp;for modeling the Distance information and the Doppler Frequency.&amp;nbsp;The output signal can be measured&amp;nbsp;by SystemVue sink model or&amp;nbsp;VSA software.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Example3 - ComplexRadarSignal&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Generates a QPSK jamming signal to test&amp;nbsp;a Radar receiver&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;.&amp;nbsp; Additional commercial PHY signals such as LTE, or recorded waveforms using a VSA or RF sensor, can be added.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Example4&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;STRONG&gt;- Radar Signal Processing&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;A Constant False Alarm Rate (CFAR) detector is created based on Cell Averaging structure.&amp;nbsp; False Alarm&amp;nbsp;Rate and Detection Rate are simulated&amp;nbsp;in two separate designs.&amp;nbsp;You have a choice of Floating or Fixed-Point Cell Averaging models.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;All the models in this example can be used as templates for custom models.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Users can open&amp;nbsp;these models and modify them&amp;nbsp;as needed to create custom models for&amp;nbsp;their own&amp;nbsp;system simulation.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="NotesDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;Rt14;am14</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;X25AKea7l24;jms2SBO}b24</D></PVPort>
